      "title": "Lecturer, Integrated Media (Public Relations)",
      "description": "Lecturer, Integrated Media (Public Relations) - Spokane, Washington, United States Lecturer, Integrated Media (Public Relations) - Spokane, Washington, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Lecturer, Integrated Media (Public Relations) Spokane, Washington, United States Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Full-time) Closing at: Oct 29 2026 - 23:55 PDT Add to favorites View favorites Title: Lecturer, Integrated Media (Public Relations) Area: College of Arts and Sciences Department: Integrated Media Telework Availability: On-campus Position Employee Classification: Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Full-time) Appointment Percentage: 100 Months per year: 9 Salary Range: The budgeted annual salary that the University reasonably expects to offer for this position is $61,905 (Lecturer-IR, rank w/o terminal degree) or $71,601 (Lecturer-AT, rank w/terminal degree). The internal salary ranges are $61,905 - $66,032 (Lecturer-IR) and $71,601 - $76,375 (Lecturer-AT), depending on degree. Is this position eligible for relocation reimbursement?: Yes Is this position eligible for a signing bonus?: No Gonzaga University evaluates request for H1-B sponsorship on a case by case basis. Sponsorship eligibility depends on the position, institutional considerations, and applicable federal immigration requirements. Job Purpose: The Integrated Media Department (Public Relations program) at Gonzaga University in Spokane, Washington, invites applications for a full-time, fixed-term, renewable non-tenure-track faculty position beginning Fall 2027. The successful candidate will be appointed at the rank of Lecturer. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses in Public Relations and build and maintain connections with local industry and the broader field. The position also includes academic and career advising, service to the department and University, and, beginning in the second year, leadership responsibilities within the Public Relations program, including program assessment and curriculum review. Gonzaga University is a Jesuit, Catholic, humanistic institution, and is therefore interested in candidates who will contribute to its distinctive mission of educating students “for lives of leadership and service for the common good.” The Integrated Media Department and the College of Arts and Sciences are committed to inclusive excellence, and the success of a diverse population of undergraduate students, staff, and faculty. Consistent with the mission values of the University, the department strives to serve its community and the world through education, scholarship, artistic expression, inclusive media practices, and professional and community engagement. The department welcomes candidates eager to contribute to our goal of inclusive excellence in teaching and to pursue professional interests in an environment that values and practices care and respect for all community members. For more information on our mission, please visit: https://www.gonzaga.edu/about/our-mission-jesuit-values/mission-statement Essential Functions: Teach the equivalent of 24 credits per academic year, including, but not limited to, Public Relations Principles and Theories, Public Relations Writing, Public Relations Speech Writing and Delivery, Media Research, and Media/PR Ethics. The regular teaching load is four courses (12 credits) per semester, with the possibility of course reassignments based on other responsibilities. Develop and maintain connections with local industry and the broader field in ways that inform teaching, enhance the student experience, and help the faculty member remain current in the field. Provide academic and career advising to Public Relations majors, beginning in the second year. Support the department and University through service and other forms of academic citizenship, including attending regular departmental and campus-wide meetings. Provide leadership within the Public Relations program, beginning in the second year, including overseeing processes such as program assessment and curriculum review. Minimum Qualifications: A master’s degree in public relations, media studies, communication, strategic communications, business administration, or a related field; a professional doctorate or discipline-specific terminal degree; dissertation-stage status in a terminal degree; or a combination of academic credentials and professional experience and expertise deemed appropriate by the department and dean. Preferred Qualifications: At least one year of undergraduate teaching experience in public relations or a similar discipline, such as strategic communication or media writing. Demonstrated ability with curriculum design, assessment, and/or academic advising. Evidence of building and maintaining connections with industry or the broader public relations profession. Educational Requirement: Master's Degree Physical & On-Campus Requirements: In-Office Presence - Ability to work on-site in typical office setting and participate in in-person meetings with colleagues: 5 days/week Standing/Sitting - Ability to remain in a stationary position for a prolonged period: Often (50%-75% of time) Walking - Ability to move about on foot to accomplish tasks: Often (50%-75% of time) Lifting/Carrying - Ability to move or transport objects up to a specified weight: Rarely (1%-49% of time) Attention to Detail - Ability to focus on detailed tasks for extended periods: Daily (>75% of time) Problem-Solving - Ability to identify and resolve issues effectively: Daily (>75% of time) Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit our website at www.gonzaga.edu/jobs • A cover letter that addresses the qualifications for appointment, the candidate’s perspective on the future of the public relations field, and the candidate’s understanding of and commitment to the University’s mission. • Curriculum vitae or resume. • A statement of teaching philosophy (2-page maximum) referencing evidence of teaching effectiveness and describing how the candidate will create and maintain an inclusive environment that can support and promote learning for students with a variety of backgrounds and identities. • Evidence of effective teaching and/or sample materials from relevant courses, if available. • Evidence of professional work, if available. • Copies of unofficial graduate school transcripts, if applicable. Names and contact information for three (3) professional references will be collected from advancing candidates during the interview process (letters of recommendation will be requested when finalists are selected). For information about the institution, visit Gonzaga on the internet at www.gonzaga.edu. For more information about inclusive excellence in the College of Arts and Sciences, visit us at www.gonzaga.edu/casjobs. Questions about the position can be directed to the Public Relations Search Committee Chair, Dr. Molly Kretchmar-Hendricks at kretchmar@gonzaga.edu. This position will close October 29, 2026 at 11:55PM (PST). For assistance with your online application, please contact Human Resources at 509.313.5996. Total Rewards Statement At Gonzaga, we value the well-being and contributions of our colleagues by offering a comprehensive total rewards package. In compliance with Washington State's Pay Transparency Act, we provide both the full salary range for each position, and an anticipated salary range that reflects the budgeted amount that the university reasonable expects to offer the position. In addition to base compensation, we offer a competitive benefits package, which may vary depending on the position type and hours worked. To explore the full range of benefits available, please review the applicable Prospective Employee Benefit Guide available on the Gonzaga website. EEO Statement Gonzaga University is a Jesuit, Catholic, humanistic institution, and is therefore interested in candidates who will contribute to its distinctive mission. Gonzaga University is a committed EEO/AA employer and diversity candidates are encouraged to apply. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their disability status and/or protected veteran status. Applicants with disabilities needing reasonable accommodations to complete the application or hiring process should contact Human Resources (509) 313-5996. Apply now First Name (required) e7a33c3c Last Name (required) 0b486175 Email (required) 76c08492 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Security Officer Spokane, Washington, United States Campus Security & Public Safety Gonzaga University's Campus Security team is hiring for a Security Officer! Head Coach - Women's Cross Country, Track & Field Spokane, Washington, United States Other Women's Sports Lead and shape a nationally competitive NCAA Division I Women's Cross Country and Track & Field program while competing in the highly competitive Pac-12 Conference. This position is responsible for all aspects of program administration, including coaching, student-athlete development, recruiting, mentoring, program planning, public relations, community engagement, and administrative oversight. The successful candidate will foster a culture of excellence on and off the track while ensuring full compliance with all University, conference, and NCAA regulations. Adjunct Instructor, Accounting (Taxation) Spokane, Washington, United States School of Business Administration Gonzaga University is seeking adjunct faculty members in the School of Business Administration to fulfill open course opportunities in the Spring 2027 semester for our Master of Science in Taxation program. Adjunct Instructor, School of Business Administration Spokane, Washington, United States School of Business Administration Gonzaga University in Spokane, Washington, is seeking adjunct faculty members in the School of Business Administration to fulfill open course opportunities in the Spring 2027 semester. Adjunct Instructor, Teacher 